        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sly Stone, Mary Ramsey\n- Bands: Sly and the Family Stone\n- Roles: musician, songwriter, record producer, frontman\n- Music genres: soul, funk, rock, psychedelia\n\nFacts:\n- Sly Stone was born as Sylvester Stewart on March 15, 1943, in Denton, Texas.\n- Sly Stone is an American musician, songwriter, and record producer.\n- Sly Stone is most famous as the frontman of Sly and the Family Stone.\n- Sly and the Family Stone played a critical role in the development of soul, funk, rock, and psychedelia in the 1960s and 1970s.\n- Mary Ramsey has worked with Jackson Browne, Goo Goo Dolls, Billy Bragg, Warren Zevon, Alex Chilton, and Ani DiFranco.",
